	abstract = {We calculate the thermal diffusion constant {DT} and butterfly velocity {vB} in neutral magnetized plasma using a holographic magnetic brane background. We find that the thermal diffusion constant satisfies Blake’s bound. The constant in the bound {DT}2{πT}/v2B is a decreasing function of magnetic field. It approaches one half in the large-magnetic-field limit. We also find the existence of a special point defined by the Lyapunov exponent and butterfly velocity at which the pole-skipping phenomenon occurs.},
